PART A — STRUCTURAL ACCESSIBILITY FIXES (apply unconditionally)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

A1. Page title
    - Ensure <title> is descriptive and page-specific
    - Format: "Page Purpose — Site Name"
    - Never leave as "index.html", "Document", or empty

A2. Landmark regions
    - Replace <div class="header"> → <header>
    - Replace <div class="nav">    → <nav aria-label="Main">
    - Replace <div class="main">   → <main>
    - Replace <div class="footer"> → <footer>
    - Replace <div class="aside">  → <aside aria-label="[descriptive label]">
    - Do not add landmarks that the page does not actually have

A3. Skip navigation
    - Add as the very first child of <body>:
      <a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
    - Add id="main-content" to the <main> element
    - Add CSS: .skip-link { position:absolute; transform:translateY(-100%); }
               .skip-link:focus { transform:translateY(0); }

A4. Heading hierarchy
    - Ensure exactly one <h1> that describes the page
    - Subheadings must follow sequential order (h1→h2→h3)
    - Replace any <div class="heading"> with the correct <hN> element
    - Heading text must be descriptive, not generic

A5. Image alternatives
    - Every <img> must have an alt attribute
    - Meaningful images: alt describes function or content ("Submit payment")
    - Decorative images: alt=""
    - Never use filename, "image", or empty string for meaningful images

A6. Form labels
    - Every <input>, <select>, <textarea> must have an associated <label>
    - Use for/id pairing or wrap input in <label>
    - Add required attribute to mandatory fields
    - Never use placeholder as the only label

A7. Interactive element labels
    - Every <button> must have descriptive text content or aria-label
    - Every <a> must have descriptive text (never "click here", "read more")
    - Icon-only buttons: add aria-label="[action description]"

A8. Language attribute
    - Ensure <html lang="en"> (or appropriate language code) is present

